  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montenegro: Strengthening Capacities of the Montenegrin National Centre for Training in the Judiciary and State Prosecution (CTJP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To optimize the CTJP&#x2019;s IT system to enhance online course training capability. 2) To create a user-friendly resource library for trainers and trainees of the CTJP. 3) To integrate training evaluation tools into the CTJP&#x2019;s e-learning platform. 4) To upgrade and regularly update the CTJP&#x2019;s electronic training records database. 5) To assist the CTJP in conducting monthly statistical reporting and attendance tracking. 6) To develop an innovative three-year strategy for 2024-2027. 7) To assist the CTJP in developing one-year training plans. 8) To support the CTJP in developing and introducing a practice-based adult learning methodology into all new curricula. 9) To assist the CTJP in identifying and certifying prospective Trainers of Trainers. 10) To enable the CTJP to provide structured training on gender, integrity, and ethics considerations to registered trainees. 11) To support the CTJP in developing a corruption and organized crime-specific e-learning curriculum. 12) To conduct a series of annual training courses for prosecutors and judges on the subjects of financial crime, corruption, organized crime, mutual legal assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiary: The Montenegrin Centre for Training in the Judiciary and State Prosecution.Indirect beneficiaries: Judges, prosecutors, and other legal professionals receiving training from the CTJP.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to increase the operational functioning of the Montenegrin Centre for Training in the Judiciary and State Prosecution (CTJP) to fulfil its mandate as intended.</narrative>
  </description>
